# OG Worker Plan execution adapter

Apply this rule only while the shared `execute-todo` or `execute-plan` Skill is active.

## Plans and branches

- This repository currently has no local Phase plan convention. Activate the shared workflow only when the user supplies or explicitly identifies an accepted plan TODO.
- Prefer branch names in the form `<type>/p<N.N>-<short-task-name>` when the plan provides a TODO number; otherwise ask before choosing a workflow branch name.
- Base independent task branches on the latest `main`.

## Verification

- Run `npm test` for behavior changes.
- Run `npm run typecheck` for TypeScript changes.
- Run `npm run dry-run` only when Worker packaging or deployment configuration changes and the required local environment is available.
- Never run `npm run deploy` without explicit deployment authorization.

## Completion

- Do not invent a plan status location or report path. Use the accepted plan's stated location; ask when absent.
- Follow recent Conventional Commit style.
- Publish through a GitHub PR and preserve required checks and branch protection.
- A matching `execute-todo` or `execute-plan` command supplies standard Git delivery authorization, including merge; deployment still requires separate explicit authorization.